    <briefdescription>
<para>Abstract listener interface for training incident events. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Implementations receive every incident emitted by <ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_training_incident_emitter" kindref="compound">TrainingIncidentEmitter</ref>. <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_training_incident_listener_1a77da47e9377ba1cf29738083aa320967" kindref="member">onIncident</ref></computeroutput> is called with the emitter&apos;s internal mutex held, so implementations MUST NOT call back into the emitter (to avoid deadlock) and SHOULD return quickly to avoid stalling the emitting thread.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Thread-safety contract</title><para>The emitter calls <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_training_incident_listener_1a77da47e9377ba1cf29738083aa320967" kindref="member">onIncident</ref></computeroutput> under a mutex. Implementations are responsible for their own internal thread safety (e.g., if they forward to a queue). </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
